{number: 26}
{title: O Little Town of Bethlehem}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] O little town of [Bb] Bethlehem,
How [F] still we [C7] see thee [F] lie!
Above thy [D7] deep and [Gm] dreamless sleep
The [F] silent [C7] stars go [F] by;
Yet [F] in thy dark streets [Dm] shin-[E7] eth
The [Am] everlasting [C] Light;
The [F] hopes and fears of [Bb] all the years
Are [F] met in [C7] thee to-[F] night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
For [F] Christ is born of [Bb] Mary;
And [F] gathered [C7] all a-[F] bove,
While [D7] mortals sleep, the [Gm] angels keep
Their [F] watch of [C7] wond'ring [F] love,
O [F] morning stars, to-[Dm] geth-[E7] er
Pro-[Am] claim the holy [C] birth!
And [F] praises sing to [Bb] God the King,
And [F] peace to [C7] men on [F] earth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
How [F] silently, how [Bb] silently,
The [F] wondrous [C7] gift is [F] giv'n!
So [D7] God imparts to [Gm] human hearts
The [F] blessings [C7] of His [F] Heav'n.
No [F] ear may hear His [Dm] com-[E7] ing;
But [Am] in this world of [C] sin,
Where [F] meek souls will re-[Bb] ceive Him still,
The [F] dear Christ [C7] enters [F] in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [F] holy Child of [Bb] Bethlehem,
De-[F] scend to [C7] us, we [F] pray;
Cast [D7] out our sin, and [Gm] enter in,
Be [F] born in [C7] us to-[F] day.
We [F] hear the Christmas [Dm] an-[E7] gels
The [Am] great glad tidings [C] tell,--
O [F] come to us, a-[Bb] bide with us,
Our [F] Lord Em-[C7] manu-[F] el.
{end_of_verse}
